<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuan Dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yuan Dynasty was the Mongol-ruled dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, proclaimed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> in 1271, which completed the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> in 1279. It made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a>, its capital, promoted trade across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurasia">Eurasia</a> and patronised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhism</a>. Weakened by factional conflict, floods, plague and rebellion, it was driven from China in 1368 by the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty.jpg" alt="Yuan Dynasty" width="320" height="337" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cattette · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuan_Dynasty_revised.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
